    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d217">

                <pb facs="0317" n="211" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg211"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Egan</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-11-01"><hi rendition="#italic">November 1,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Blaine instructs Mr. Egan to claim the privilege of reading the paper which
                    the American sailors have signed in secret, in a language they did not
                    understand, and without being accompanied by counsel, and to see that no one
                    from the <hi rendition="#italic">Baltimore</hi>, officer or sailor, is allowed
                    to testify except in the presence of a friend acting as counsel and in his own
                    language openly and not secretly.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
